Why this grant exists
---------------------
These files are ground truth for a public evaluation benchmark. A benchmark
whose data cannot be redistributed cannot be independently reproduced, and a
number nobody else can reproduce is not a result. Keeping the server under
AGPL-3.0 protects the tooling; releasing the data it is measured against
under MIT lets anyone check the numbers.

Scope
-----
This grant covers data, fixtures and example inputs only. It relicenses no
source code, and it does not affect the AGPL-3.0 obligations that attach to
running or conveying this server, including the network-use obligation in
AGPL-3.0 section 13.


